WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:00.967
Payton Walsh.

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:03.169
He's in the Ukrainian capital of Kyiv.

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.137
Nick, what more?

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:04.537
First of all,

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.139
can you tell us about General

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:08.074
Sir of ICANN's relationship

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:09.876
with the head of the group

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:12.512
whose whereabouts are also murky tonight?

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:16.049
Yeah, I mean, as you say,

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:17.083
we don't know where he is.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:18.318
He hasn't been seen in public

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:20.420
since that video you just saw on Friday

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.054
where he appealed

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:22.956
to foreign mercenaries to turn around

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:23.957
and not advance

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:25.592
continue their advance towards Moscow.

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:26.993
There have been some media reports

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:28.495
suggesting that he may indeed

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:29.763
have been detained,

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:30.597
some suggesting

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:32.032
he may indeed have been arrested.

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:33.633
But a Russian official

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:34.801
with severe knowledge

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.069
of the pretrial detention

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:36.469
prison

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:39.472
system says that he's not in that system.

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:41.341
So a lot of uncertainty

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:41.941
as to exactly

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:43.576
whether he has been interrogated

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.078
and let go or quite

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:45.845
where he is

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:46.913
was pretty clear

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:48.348
is he's not going to be happy

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:50.083
to hear about reports

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:52.485
of being a VIP member of whatever

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:53.086
that means.

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:54.687
There's something you apply for or get

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.923
given unilaterally.

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:59.726
But also, Prigozhin himself, frankly,

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:01.861
was the only the only command

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:02.762
in the Russian military.

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:04.564
He spoke highly of or complimentary

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:07.033
of was indeed, Sue Rivkin.

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:07.567
So clearly,

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.302
the men were relatively close

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:11.004
and precautions of darkness

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:12.439
sort of rose to the incident.

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:13.706
See while

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:16.276
Rivkin was running the Ukraine war.

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:17.877
But really above all of this, Wolf,

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:19.179
whatever the truth of the matter

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:20.513
of all these bits

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:22.749
of kompromat, compromising information

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:23.850
being given out

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.485
about the Russian top brass,

00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:27.687
it just speaks to the utter disunity

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:29.222
that will be currently taking place

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:29.622
with inside

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:30.824
the Russian Ministry of Defense

00:01:30.824 --> 00:01:31.958
and the Kremlin.

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:33.626
They are clearly on a bit of a witch

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:34.294
hunt now,

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:36.329
trying to work out who knew in advance

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:38.798
who didn't do enough to stop

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:41.534
what's been called the march of justice

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:42.702
towards Moscow.

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:45.905
And that is exactly what here in Kiev

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:47.941
they are keen to see expand.

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:48.708
But also what

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:50.610
a country in a disastrous war

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.278
like Russia does not need.

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:52.979
They're going to have to make

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:54.147
some difficult choices

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:55.515
on the battlefield soon.

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:56.583
But it seems right now

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:57.750
they're far too busy

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.252
pointing the finger at each other.

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:01.087
While Putin himself

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:02.055
appears to be less

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:03.690
and less calling the shots.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.125
Nick, stick around.

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:06.960
I'll get back to you in a few moments.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.595
I also want to bring in retired U.S.

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:09.963
General Spider Marks.

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:12.398
He's a CNN military analyst General.

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:13.933
Let me get your reaction,

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:15.602
first of all, to this exclusive

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:17.704
new reporting from Matthew Chance.

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:19.973
Documents suggesting General

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:23.743
Sara weaken was a secret member of the

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:25.178
Wagner mercenary group

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:28.781
Wolf,

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:29.349
you know, what that

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:30.250
tells me

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.885
is that there's this

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:33.419
what we've suspected all along,

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:34.721
this cancer of corruption

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:36.055
within minimally

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:37.190
within the ministry of defense.

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:38.191
But clearly

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:39.993
throughout all those elements

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:40.560
of governance

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.295
within the Russian Federation,

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:44.464
I mean, how can a professional soldier,

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:46.099
a professional soldier

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:47.433
also have

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:48.501
a relationship,

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:50.970
obviously a fiduciary relationship

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:53.339
with a paramilitary group,

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:54.707
if nothing else,

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:57.610
it talks about really lousy tradecraft.

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:58.711
I mean, if you're going to try

00:02:58.711 --> 00:02:59.746
to have a secretive

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:00.713
relationship, don't

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:02.348
sign up for a membership card,

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:04.150
which is exactly what he did.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:07.353
It really speaks to the fragility.

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:08.288
As Nick

00:03:08.288 --> 00:03:09.522
Paton Walsh just indicated,

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:10.790
the real fragility

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.258
within the Ministry of Defense

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:13.726
in terms of what other heads

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:14.627
are going to fall.

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:16.362
Who truly is in charge

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:17.730
and who's going to step up

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:20.266
in order to advance what Russia sees

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:22.202
as a legitimate effort on their part

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:23.403
in Ukraine?

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:24.804
Let me get back to Nick.

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:25.805
Nick, Putin

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:28.174
maybe looking for scapegoats right now

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:29.242
after that mutiny,

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:31.844
but are there risks to making Prigozhin

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.546
and sir, a vegan, for that matter,

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:34.547
into martyrs?

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:38.184
Well, that was ultimately, I

00:03:38.184 --> 00:03:39.586
think, what was in the background

00:03:39.586 --> 00:03:41.721
as we saw this sort of extraordinary

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:44.791
lack of military and political opposition

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:45.725
to Prigozhin

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:47.160
as he marched on the weekend

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.494
up towards Moscow.

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:49.963
I think most people interpreted

00:03:49.963 --> 00:03:51.130
that as perhaps the Kremlin

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.999
simply not being sure

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:54.367
that if they really went

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:55.735
for Prigozhin and his men,

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:57.103
that they had the strength

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:58.037
to take them on,

00:03:58.037 --> 00:04:00.173
but also to that they might actually find

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:01.975
that essentially improve their position

00:04:01.975 --> 00:04:02.875
because they would be asking

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:04.711
the Russian military to turn on Vadim,

00:04:04.711 --> 00:04:05.912
who done so much of the fierce

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:08.214
fighting on the Ukrainian front line,

00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:09.515
very brutal as they are

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:11.351
over the past year or so.

00:04:11.351 --> 00:04:13.353
So enormous question, frankly,

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:13.653
as to what

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:14.887
this residual support

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:16.723
potentially for both men

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:18.057
may be within the military.

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:18.324
Sort of

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:20.093
he can was a man who was respected,

00:04:20.093 --> 00:04:20.994
I think is fair to say,

00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:22.195
inside the military.

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:24.364
And many of Russia's key battlefields,

00:04:24.364 --> 00:04:26.366
including Syria over the past years.

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:27.834
And Prigozhin, despite being.

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:28.434
I think it's fair to say

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.403
pretty mouthy, pretty bombastic,

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:31.938
certainly to lead a group

00:04:31.938 --> 00:04:34.307
which held back moot, fought for back.

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:35.341
And so I think

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:36.542
ultimately what Putin is left

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:38.978
dealing with now is a military

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:39.946
that's divided.

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:40.413
A military

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:41.814
that may be questioning quite

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:43.383
what his motivations are

00:04:43.383 --> 00:04:44.584
and the military to maybe

00:04:44.584 --> 00:04:46.119
looking at some of their top brass,

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:46.653
like sort of

00:04:46.653 --> 00:04:48.321
he can get people like Prigozhin

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:49.188
and seeing them

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:50.823
possibly being persecuted.

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:52.292
Prigozhin almost certainly.

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:53.960
And wondering what that says about

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.361
Putin's own motivation.

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:55.862
Remember,

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:57.497
he chose to fight this war,

00:04:57.497 --> 00:04:58.765
an invasion of choice.

00:04:58.765 --> 00:05:00.833
It's gone pretty catastrophically wrong.

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:02.702
And tens of thousands of Russians

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:03.770
have lost their lives.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:04.971
That's going to be making a mark

00:05:04.971 --> 00:05:05.972
on the personal lives

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:07.740
of many Russian families.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:08.408
And so I think we're

00:05:08.408 --> 00:05:09.542
at an inflection point,

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:10.610
certainly in the days

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:12.512
ahead to see quite how this plays

00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:14.080
out of Russian Putin's

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.149
grip on the military, on the Kremlin.

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:17.884
And that, of course, here in Ukraine

00:05:17.884 --> 00:05:19.152
is what they are relishing,

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:21.220
what they're waiting for, and may explain

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:22.922
why we haven't seen a sudden surge

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:24.824
in Ukrainian forces on the battlefield.

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:26.592
They're just watching this play out

00:05:26.592 --> 00:05:27.360
because each day

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:29.128
it seems that the military

00:05:29.128 --> 00:05:30.196
are turning on each other

00:05:30.196 --> 00:05:31.597
rather than fighting harder here.

00:05:31.597 --> 00:05:33.032
Yes, very dramatic indeed.

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:34.000
Nick, Paton Walsh.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.968
Retired General Marks, guys, thank you

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:36.636
very much.

